    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1381">

                <pb facs="1079" n="963" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg963"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.11/111.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 6, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I am informed by the Minister for Foreign Affairs that all the border claims have
                    now been examined. He considers that some of them are exorbitant and a few
                    untenable. But in order to avoid Congressional action at Washington he wishes to
                    pay the majority of the awards as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
